devicetree.resource/--background--         devicetree.resource/--background--

   VERSION MARKS
	The calls of this resource are described one by one below. This entry
	says since when each exists, and how a change is told, as the autodocs
	of the system do (see exec.library/AllocPooled or StackSwap).

	A call that was added after the first version of the resource has its
	version at the end of the line of its NAME, like "(V1.7)": the number is
	the version of the resource in which it appeared. A change in what a call
	does is written in its FUNCTION text, "As of V1.7 ..." and "Prior to V1.7
	...". A call without a version in its NAME has been there since 1.0.

   VERSIONS
	The history comes from the repository of the project and from the one
	that it was taken out of (Emu68-tools-old).

	1.0   2021-10-02  First version: DT_OpenKey, DT_CloseKey, DT_GetChild,
	                  DT_FindProperty, DT_GetProperty, DT_GetPropLen,
	                  DT_GetPropName and DT_GetPropValue.
	1.1   2021-10-03  The set-up checks the pointers that it gets back.
	1.2   2021-10-05  DT_GetParent added. DT_OpenKey resolves a whole path
	                  (see DT_OpenKey).
	1.3   2021-12-15  Memory that exec has not added yet is added by the
	                  resource at start-up. No call changed. This one is
	                  only a revision: the project still said 1.2.
	1.4   2022-11-04  DT_GetKeyName added.
	1.5   2024-01-05  DT_FindPropertyRecursive added. The calls were cleaned
	                  up, what they do is the same.
	1.6   2025-11-04  The messages of the set-up go through bug(), the
	                  debug port of Emu68. No call changed.

	The ROM of the Emu68 1.1.0-beta.1 build of 17.10.2026 has 1.5, built
	from the tree of commit 943f3b5.

   VERSION AND REVISION
	lib_Version and lib_Revision of the resource. They were written by hand
	and did not always follow the id string: the project said 1.2 while the
	revision was 3, and from 1.5 on the revision stayed at 4 while the id
	string said 1.5. So a resource of 1.4 and one of 1.5 both have
	lib_Revision 4, and the second has "devicetree 1.5" as its id string.
	From 1.6 the id string, lib_Version and lib_Revision all come from the
	version of the project (1.6 gives lib_Version 1 and lib_Revision 6).

	A program that needs DT_FindPropertyRecursive (V1.5) cannot tell a 1.5
	from a 1.4 by lib_Revision. It can by the size of the table of vectors:
	lib_NegSize is at least 11 * 6 = 66 with that call, 60 without it.

   SEE ALSO
	exec.library/OpenResource()

devicetree.resource/DT_CloseKey               devicetree.resource/DT_CloseKey

   NAME
	DT_CloseKey -- close a node obtained with DT_OpenKey

   SYNOPSIS
	DT_CloseKey( key )
	             a0

	VOID DT_CloseKey(APTR);

   FUNCTION
	Closes a key. This is a no-op today, since the tree is never
	freed, but call it anyway for forward compatibility.

   INPUTS
	key             A node returned by DT_OpenKey().

   SEE ALSO
	devicetree.resource/DT_OpenKey()

devicetree.resource/DT_FindProperty       devicetree.resource/DT_FindProperty

   NAME
	DT_FindProperty -- find a property of a node by name

   SYNOPSIS
	property = DT_FindProperty( key, property )
	d0                          a0   a1

	APTR DT_FindProperty(APTR, CONST_STRPTR);

   FUNCTION
	Searches the properties of a node for one with exactly the given
	name. The parents are not searched.

   INPUTS
	key             The node to search. NULL returns NULL.
	property        Name of the property, e.g. "compatible".

   RESULTS
	property        The property, or NULL if the node has none by that
	                name.

   EXAMPLES
	#include <proto/exec.h>
	#include <proto/devicetree.h>

	APTR DeviceTreeBase = OpenResource("devicetree.resource");
	if (DeviceTreeBase)
	{
	    APTR key = DT_OpenKey("/");
	    APTR prop = DT_FindProperty(key, "model");

	    if (prop)
	        Printf("%s\n", DT_GetPropValue(prop));
	}

   SEE ALSO
	devicetree.resource/DT_FindPropertyRecursive(),
	devicetree.resource/DT_GetPropValue()

devicetree.resource/DT_FindPropertyRecursive devicetree.resource/DT_FindPropertyRecursive

   NAME
	DT_FindPropertyRecursive -- find a property in a node or in its ancestors (V1.5)

   SYNOPSIS
	property = DT_FindPropertyRecursive( key, property )
	d0                                   a0   a1

	APTR DT_FindPropertyRecursive(APTR, CONST_STRPTR);

   FUNCTION
	Like DT_FindProperty(), but when the node has no such property
	the search goes on with its parent, up to the root node. Useful
	for inherited properties such as "#address-cells".

   INPUTS
	key             The node to start from.
	property        Name of the property.

   RESULTS
	property        The nearest property found, or NULL if no node up to
	                the root has it.

   SEE ALSO
	devicetree.resource/DT_FindProperty(),
	devicetree.resource/DT_GetParent()

devicetree.resource/DT_GetChild               devicetree.resource/DT_GetChild

   NAME
	DT_GetChild -- get the first child of a node, or the next sibling

   SYNOPSIS
	child = DT_GetChild( key, prev )
	d0                   a0   a1

	APTR DT_GetChild(APTR, APTR);

   FUNCTION
	Iterates over the children of a node. With prev set to NULL the
	first child is returned; with prev set to a previous result the
	next sibling is returned.

   INPUTS
	key             Parent node. NULL means the root node.
	prev            The child returned by the previous call, or NULL to
	                start.

   RESULTS
	child           The child, or NULL at the end of the list.

   EXAMPLES
	#include <proto/exec.h>
	#include <proto/devicetree.h>

	APTR DeviceTreeBase = OpenResource("devicetree.resource");
	if (DeviceTreeBase)
	{
	    APTR key = DT_OpenKey("/soc");
	    APTR child = NULL;

	    while (child = DT_GetChild(key, child))
	        Printf("%s\n", DT_GetKeyName(child));
	}

   SEE ALSO
	devicetree.resource/DT_GetParent(),
	devicetree.resource/DT_GetKeyName()

devicetree.resource/DT_GetKeyName           devicetree.resource/DT_GetKeyName

   NAME
	DT_GetKeyName -- get the name of a node (V1.4)

   SYNOPSIS
	name = DT_GetKeyName( key )
	d0                    a0

	CONST_STRPTR DT_GetKeyName(APTR);

   FUNCTION
	Returns the name of a node, including its unit address if any
	("serial@7e201000").

   INPUTS
	key             A node. NULL returns an empty string.

   RESULTS
	name            The name; never NULL. The root node has an empty name.

   SEE ALSO
	devicetree.resource/DT_OpenKey()

devicetree.resource/DT_GetParent             devicetree.resource/DT_GetParent

   NAME
	DT_GetParent -- get the parent of a node (V1.2)

   SYNOPSIS
	parent = DT_GetParent( key )
	d0                     a0

	APTR DT_GetParent(APTR);

   FUNCTION
	Returns the node which contains the given node.

   INPUTS
	key             The node. NULL is taken as the root node.

   RESULTS
	parent          The parent, or NULL for the root node. Note that
	                DT_GetParent(NULL) returns the root node itself.

   SEE ALSO
	devicetree.resource/DT_GetChild()

devicetree.resource/DT_GetProperty         devicetree.resource/DT_GetProperty

   NAME
	DT_GetProperty -- get the first property of a node, or the next one

   SYNOPSIS
	property = DT_GetProperty( key, prev )
	d0                         a0   a1

	APTR DT_GetProperty(APTR, APTR);

   FUNCTION
	Iterates over the properties of a node. With prev set to NULL
	the first property is returned; with prev set to a previous
	result the next property is returned.

   INPUTS
	key             The node. NULL means the root node.
	prev            The property returned by the previous call, or NULL to
	                start.

   RESULTS
	property        The property, or NULL at the end of the list.

   EXAMPLES
	#include <proto/exec.h>
	#include <proto/devicetree.h>

	APTR DeviceTreeBase = OpenResource("devicetree.resource");
	if (DeviceTreeBase)
	{
	    APTR key = DT_OpenKey("/");
	    APTR prop = NULL;

	    while (prop = DT_GetProperty(key, prop))
	        Printf("%s (%ld bytes)\n", DT_GetPropName(prop), DT_GetPropLen(prop));
	}

   SEE ALSO
	devicetree.resource/DT_FindProperty(),
	devicetree.resource/DT_GetPropName()

devicetree.resource/DT_GetPropLen           devicetree.resource/DT_GetPropLen

   NAME
	DT_GetPropLen -- get the size of a property value

   SYNOPSIS
	length = DT_GetPropLen( property )
	d0                      a0

	ULONG DT_GetPropLen(APTR);

   FUNCTION
	Returns the length in bytes of the value of a property. A
	property without value (a flag) has a length of 0.

   INPUTS
	property        A property. NULL returns 0.

   RESULTS
	length          Size of the value in bytes.

   SEE ALSO
	devicetree.resource/DT_GetPropValue()

devicetree.resource/DT_GetPropName         devicetree.resource/DT_GetPropName

   NAME
	DT_GetPropName -- get the name of a property

   SYNOPSIS
	name = DT_GetPropName( property )
	d0                     a0

	CONST_STRPTR DT_GetPropName(APTR);

   FUNCTION
	Returns the name of a property.

   INPUTS
	property        A property. NULL returns an empty string.

   RESULTS
	name            The name; never NULL.

   SEE ALSO
	devicetree.resource/DT_GetProperty()

devicetree.resource/DT_GetPropValue       devicetree.resource/DT_GetPropValue

   NAME
	DT_GetPropValue -- get the value of a property

   SYNOPSIS
	value = DT_GetPropValue( property )
	d0                       a0

	CONST_APTR DT_GetPropValue(APTR);

   FUNCTION
	Returns a pointer to the raw value of a property, as stored in
	the device tree blob.

   INPUTS
	property        A property. NULL returns NULL.

   RESULTS
	value           The value, or NULL if the property has none.

   NOTE
	Integers (cells) are big-endian 32-bit words, as in any
	flattened device tree. Strings are NUL-terminated. The size is
	given by DT_GetPropLen().

   SEE ALSO
	devicetree.resource/DT_GetPropLen()

devicetree.resource/DT_OpenKey                 devicetree.resource/DT_OpenKey

   NAME
	DT_OpenKey -- open a node by its path

   SYNOPSIS
	key = DT_OpenKey( name )
	d0                a0

	APTR DT_OpenKey(CONST_STRPTR);

   FUNCTION
	Looks up a node of the device tree from its absolute path. The
	path starts at the root node ("/"), node names are separated by
	"/".

	A name without unit address ("serial") also matches a node named
	with one ("serial@7e201000"). A path component is limited to 63
	characters.

	As of V1.2 the whole path is resolved, one component after the other,
	and NULL is returned as soon as one is not found. Prior to V1.2 every
	component was looked for in the children of the root and the first one
	found was returned: DT_OpenKey("/soc/gpio") gave the node "soc", not
	"gpio".

   INPUTS
	name            Absolute path of the node, e.g. "/soc/gpio". "/" is
	                the root.

   RESULTS
	key             The node, or NULL if the path is not absolute or a
	                component was not found.

   EXAMPLES
	#include <proto/exec.h>
	#include <proto/devicetree.h>

	APTR DeviceTreeBase = OpenResource("devicetree.resource");
	if (DeviceTreeBase)
	{
	    APTR key = DT_OpenKey("/soc");
	    if (key)
	    {
	        /* ... */
	        DT_CloseKey(key);
	    }
	}

   NOTE
	The device tree is read-only and always resident: a key stays
	valid until reboot.

   SEE ALSO
	devicetree.resource/DT_CloseKey()

